  "adaptations": [
    "Actual native preorder plus retained sibling indices/children supply node links without registration or layout ordering.",
    "Owned nodes/maps are immutable; original value, rendered content, props, renderer and caller ref identities remain in JavaScript.",
    "Preserve lookup membership versus linked navigation, item-only size, source duplicate-key replacement and changed-ID rejection, source at/childNodes exceptions and numeric-zero filtering edge.",
    "No react-aria, DOM, browser or test runtime import is added to native.",
    "Private descriptor owners allocate generated keys/revisions only in committed effects and expose wire revisions in a subsequent native commit; discarded render drafts publish nothing.",
    "An independently committed native root ref binds receipt authority. Previous complete renderer membership survives pending receipts and whole-Activity rebinding; it grants no native business-action authority.",
    "Private metadata identities/targets live in a WeakMap sidecar and are absent from renderer-facing node objects.",
    "The source object cache, dependency/id-scope precedence, original values/renderers/refs, one-shot iteration, and retained node-label behavior are preserved.",
    "Visible business operations require an original current native acknowledgement of the exact metadata lease, retained descriptor and actual visible host binding; queued stale leases retire without business callbacks.",
    "Full source state uses the separately recorded native-owned stately backend. Native renderer root/branch contexts retain complete membership, actual scroll refs, persisted keys, layout/drop delegates and source drop-indicator recursion.",
    "Pinned slot lookup, null-slot isolation, callback order, caller precedence and style/ref merging use native styles and original actual native refs. Typed business keys retain their identity while private React reconciliation keys distinguish numeric and string siblings.",
    "TagGroup uses the logical collection independently of visible row registration; offscreen requests wait for materialization and only original focus callbacks establish observed native focus. Native semantics bind actual SDK collection/table/cell properties; installed virtualization, profiles and whole-family acceptance remain open.",
    "Logical focusedKey records the source navigation intent before materialization; native command completion remains an original focus callback. Persist logical/requested/last-observed keys and cancel retired-window requests without replay."
  ],
